  "body": "Follow-up to #261 and PR #861. Generators that refuse part-way now hand back their partial path as the display-only ghost. Both match sites now handle the `Ghosted` variant, and the ghost's colour uses #698's ground-aware dimming.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Part-way refusals carry their moves.** There is a new `GenError::with_ghost_moves(&[Move])`, which is `with_ghost` over a builder's moves. Every adoption is one `map_err` / `.with_ghost..` on an **error path**. No generator finishes early or changes its control flow. The ghosts are in the generator's own frame, which `run_job` already maps to world through `world_path` (a 3+2 tilt) or which is world already.\n\n| Generator | Refusal | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2D Contour (`contour_impl`) | control comp with no lead-in/out; `push_span` | ghost added: rings so far |\n| Bore | per-hole pass budget (`cut_levels`) | ghost added: holes bored so far |\n| Circular | per-ring pass budget | ghost added: rings so far |\n| Trochoidal slot | level emit (helix-turn cap); loops cross themselves | ghost added: levels so far / the finished path |\n| 3-D ladder (Pocket3D, Multi-Axis Rough) | `hsm::plan_level` adaptive level refusal | ghost added (Rotary Offset still drops it, `without_ghost`) |\n| Plasma profile | no cut, G41 span off its cut, cover and kerf laws, torch spans | ghost added: contours so far / the whole cut |\n| Probing | touch not toward its target | ghost added: the built cycle |\n| Turning form | crown on or through the axis | ghost added: valleys so far |\n| Turning groove (blade) | rung budget per station | ghost added: stations so far |\n| Before any move (parameter, region and tool doors; bore and thread-mill hole checks) | | listed: nothing built |\n| \"Path left the finite horizon\" tails (all generators) | | listed: `Ghost::of` drops non-finite moves by law |\n| Drilling cycles (axial, radial) | per-hole doors | listed: each already names the hole's mouth (#261 part 2); the earlier holes are plunges elsewhere |\n| Rotary Offset inner ladder | | listed: wrap space, on purpose |\n| Trochoidal slot lifted-return trial | | listed: the `trial` is a scratch level, not the path |\n| Boundary turn mid-rotation | | listed: half-rotated moves, no frame |\n| finishing3d raster/rings/swarf, rotary links/posing, Face under an area turn, cross drill app-side laws, nested (already-ghosted) refusals, multiaxis stamp/swarf/curve, rotary gate, fixture route | | listed as owed: each needs a frame map or a ghost merge first; follow-up issue #1015 |\n\nThe full reasoning is in `docs/decisions/871-refusal-ghost-rest.md`.\n\n**Match sites.**\n- `cross_spindle::in_world`: a `Ghosted` refusal has its sentence rewritten and its spot moved by the hole shift, and its moves are carried by the same translation. With no shift to read, or a ghost holding an arc, the ghost and spot are dropped. Nothing is ever drawn in the spindle frame.\n- `picks::door_refusal`: reads a `Ghosted` refusal's words like the plain `Invalid` one. The pick shows words only.\n- Also found: `body_judged::name_enclosure` rewrote only `Invalid`/`At`, so a ghost-carrying holder refusal would have lost its \"(enclosure)\" words. It now goes through `GenError::map_msg`.\n\n**Colour.** The ghost uses #698's ground-aware dimming (`ground_ink::dimmed`, and `ground_ink::faded`, its light half now public for a caller's own share):\n- Dark ground: unchanged, byte for byte.\n- Light ground: the ghost fades toward the ground and never toward black. Cutting moves keep 0.9 of the gouge colour and clear WCAG 3:1 on the light viewport in every colour-vision palette (3.12:1 for the house palette; `dimmed`'s 0.6 would read 2.26:1). Rapids take `dimmed`'s 0.6, fainter still.\n\nNo snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Tests (pinning)\n- `refusal_ghost::tests::the_ghost_reads_on_the_light_ground_and_keeps_its_dark_tones` (ui lib): the light-ground contrast test. The dark tones are unchanged, the light tones lie between the gouge ink and the ground, cut ≥ 3:1, rapid fainter, never a path colour.\n- `a_part_way_refusal_hands_back_the_holes_bored_before_it` (motion `refusal_ghost`): bore refuses hole 2 with hole 1's moves as its ghost. A refusal at hole 1 carries none, with the same words.\n- `operation::cross_spindle::tests::a_ghosted_kernel_refusal_lands_its_words_spot_and_moves_in_the_world` (app lib).\n- `operation::picks::tests::a_ghosted_door_refusal_is_read_like_the_plain_one` (app lib).\n- `a_law_that_keeps_the_cylinder_names_it` (app `tool_body_judged`): extended with the ghosted case.\n- `trochoid_bore_past_the_helix_turn_cap_is_refused` (motion `trochoid_slot`): now also accepts the `Ghosted` variant of the same refusal.\n\n## Gate\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: green (motion, app, ui suites; 5.9 min)\n- `golden_cl` (6), `conformance` (25), app `refusal_ghost` (4): green. **The goldens are byte-identical.**\n- The #861 suites, motion `refusal_ghost` and ui `refusal_ghost_tests`: green.\n- Also run: motion `machining2d`, `machining3d`, `tiny_step`, `offset_shells`, `ruling`, `turning_face`, `posed_subtract`, `trochoid_slot`; app `operations`, `tool_body_judged`. All green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Visual check on screen. The colour is pinned by the unit test only, and snapshots are release-lane.\n- Ghost-carrying refusals for the circular, contour push_span, ladder, plasma, probing and turning sites are not each pinned by their own trigger. Each is a one-line `map_err` on an error path; bore pins the mechanism.\n- `contour.rs` (430 lines) and `trochoid_slot.rs` (401 lines) were already over 400 lines before this change; it adds 4 and 2 lines to them.\n\nChangelog: A refused generation that stops part-way (contour, bore, circular, trochoidal slot, 3-D ladder levels, plasma, probing, turning form and groove) now shows the moves it had built as the dashed ghost. The ghost reads on the light viewport (#871).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.17.0.\n\nFixes #871\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
